# The part of leapfrog-energy-step-gpu.test that only a release runs: all
# 17 cases of Inputs/leapfrog_energy_step.py on a GPU, in double and in
# mixed precision, of which the default test runs three, one for each form
# of the step. Under leapfrog a step that writes a row of energies leaves
# the state of the plain step to the bit (#285), and in double precision
# the positions are those of velocity Verlet within 1e-11 nm where it
# takes the same steps.
#
# It runs when lit is given -Drelease=1, as the suite of
# scripts/release/publish.sh is (docs/workflow.md, Releases).
#
# REQUIRES: hdf5, cuda, release-tests
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/leapfrog_energy_step.py mdir %S/Inputs %t/double GPU DOUBLE | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/leapfrog_energy_step.py mdir %S/Inputs %t/mixed GPU MIXED | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED

# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE nve: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE nve-free: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale: the states are identical
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE nose-hoover: the states are identical
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE langevin: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE langevin-free: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE langevin-trotter: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE langevin-trotter-first-order: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-trotter: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-trotter-first-order: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-exact: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-first-order: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE nose-hoover-trotter: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-semi-isotropic: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-anisotropic: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-anisotropic-exact: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE langevin-anisotropic: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: leapfrog GPU DOUBLE: 17 of 17 cases passed

# MIXED: GPU MIXED nve: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED nve-free: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED nose-hoover: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED langevin: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED langevin-free: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED langevin-trotter: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED langevin-trotter-first-order: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-trotter: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-trotter-first-order: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-exact: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-first-order: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED nose-hoover-trotter: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-semi-isotropic: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-anisotropic: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-anisotropic-exact: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED langevin-anisotropic: the states are identical
# MIXED: leapfrog GPU MIXED: 17 of 17 cases passed
